{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the voice was heard, etc., saying, etc.</b> That is, since Scripture had already informed us above that Egypt and the house of Pharaoh heard concerning the weeping of Joseph, as it is written (Genesis 45:2) ״וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ מִצְרַיִם״ etc., Scripture now informs us that the voice which the house of Pharaoh heard as mentioned above — and they did not know what it was or what it was about — they now told them that this was on account of the arrival of Joseph's brothers." "<b>And it was pleasing in the eyes of, etc.</b> That is, for previously there was a disgrace upon them, for a slave was ruling. But with the arrival of his brothers, it was pleasing in his eyes, for he recognized that he is not a slave."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:53.912924198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}